        <p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p>
        <h2>A good café hidden behind a bad website.</h2>
        <p>Foxtail's old site was a template with a PDF menu, no mobile ordering, and a Google profile that listed the wrong opening hours. Weekend staff were spending hours on the phone that should have gone to service.</p>
        <p>The brief was simple: make it easy for a customer to see the menu, order, and find the café — on a phone, in the language they prefer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal" style="--d:80ms">
        <p class="eyebrow">The approach</p>
        <h2>One clear action on every screen.</h2>
        <p>We started from the menu, not the homepage. Every layout was tested against three tasks: order for collection, check allergens, find the café. Content is structured so AI search can read the menu and hours directly.</p>
        <p>Built with modern AI tooling, reviewed by hand, and handed over with the code, domain and analytics all in the client's name.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

